omes in contact with damaged\nendothelium?\n…………………………………………………………", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1249}, {"number": 11, "prompt": "Who are the asymptomatic carriers in the case of hemophilia?", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1370}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "Which is the least bleeding site in factor VIII deficiency cases?\n………………………………………………………….", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 23}, {"number": 13, "prompt": "What is the treatment of choice for mild and moderate hemophilia A?\n……………………………………………………………", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 127}, {"number": 14, "prompt": "Which is the most common factor deficiency disorder around the globe?\n……………………………………………………………..", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 233}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "Hemophilia B is also called as ………………….", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 540}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "A joint which has had repeated bleeds is called as ………………….", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 587}, {"number": 17, "prompt": "One third of patients with severe hemophilia A develop alloantibody\n………………….", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 654}, {"number": 18, "prompt": "The incidence of hemophilia B is predicted to be nearly, one case per\n………………. births.", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 745}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "Hemophilia is an …………………. recessive disorder.", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 845}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "……………….. synthesize high levels of tissue factor pathway inhibitors,\nwhich predisposes hemolytic joints to bleed.", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 898}, {"number": 1, "prompt": "According to the passage, when it constitutes malpractice?\nA. if the breach of duty o f a nurse cause no harm to the patient.\nB. when a nurse commit omission during the patient care.\nC. when an action of a nurse causes damage to the patient.", "sourcePage": 8, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 33}, {"number": 4, "prompt": "Irrational use of medicines is a major global problem because?\nA. Medicine are over used by 50% of all patients\nB. inappropriate use of medicine results in destruction of insufficient resources and\nprevalent health hazards.\nC. Injections are over used instead of oral formulations to treat non-bacterial\ninfections.", "sourcePage": 11, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0}], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e", "filename": "5-watermark.pdf", "sha256": "a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [21, 22]}], "passages": []}, {"id": "a27dd3ea964dfac5-p14", "label": "Part C · 5-watermark.pdf", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e", "pages": [14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20], "questions": [{"number": 9, "prompt": "According to the passage(s), symptoms of Addison’s disease occur\nA. Slowly\nB. Suddenly\nC. After a month\nD. Slowly after many months", "sourcePage": 16, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 450, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e", "filename": "5-watermark.pdf", "sha256": "a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 22}}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "According to the information given in the passage, the statement that\n“Androgen influences muscle mass and physical and mental nature of men and\nwomen” is\nA. True\nB. False\nC. Can’t say\nD. Not given in the passage(s)", "sourcePage": 16, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 779, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e", "filename": "5-watermark.pdf", "sha256": "a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 22}}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "According to the passage, CTS\nA. is a cumulative trauma disorder\nB. is caused due to weakness in musculoskeletal system\nC. occurs due to weakness in ligaments between joints\nD. all of the above", "sourcePage": 19, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 990, "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"id": "offline-a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e", "filename": "5-watermark.pdf", "sha256": "a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 22}}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "According to the information given, CTS\nA. is on the rise\nB. is on the rise without any other cumulative trauma disorders\nC. is one of the common cumulative trauma disorders that is on rise\nD. is on the rise with many other cumulative trauma disorders", "sourcePage": 19, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 1189, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e", "filename": "5-watermark.pdf", "sha256": "a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, "page": 22}}], "skills": ["listening", "reading", "writing", "speaking"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e", "filename": "5-watermark.pdf", "sha256": "a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/a27dd3ea964dfac5fe6e3719ddd04bc277b0f6ffeab9fc4ca558294c4b85ce8e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [21, 22]}], "passages": []}]}
